Input: {"question": "What type of aircraft was involved in Flight 109?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d00", "start": 0, "end": 183, "text": "Aeroflot Flight 109 Aeroflot Flight 109 ( \"Reys 109 Aeroflota\") was a scheduled domestic passenger flight from Moscow to Chita with stopovers in Chelyabinsk, Novosibirsk, and Irkutsk."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d00", "start": 184, "end": 374, "text": "On the final leg of the route on 18 May 1973 a terrorist hijacked the aircraft, demanding to be flown to China; the terrorist's bomb detonated in flight after he was shot by the air marshal."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d00", "start": 375, "end": 469, "text": "The aircraft involved in the accident was a Tupolev Tu-104A registered CCCP-42379 to Aeroflot."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d00", "start": 470, "end": 605, "text": "The cabin layout originally had enough seats for 70 passengers, but the seating configuration was changed to accommodate 85 passengers."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d00", "start": 606, "end": 624, "text": "The Tupolev Tu-104"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d01", "start": 0, "end": 245, "text": "Last stopover Irkutsk Airport , Irkutsk Destination Kadala Airport , Chita Occupants 81 Passengers 72 Crew 9 Fatalities 81 Survivors 0 Close Aircraft The aircraft involved in the accident was a Tupolev Tu-104A registered CCCP-42379 to Aeroflot ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d01", "start": 246, "end": 383, "text": "The cabin layout originally had enough seats for 70 passengers , but the seating configuration was changed to accommodate 85 passengers ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d01", "start": 384, "end": 441, "text": "The Tupolev Tu-104 took its first flight on 17 May 1958 ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d01", "start": 442, "end": 548, "text": "At the time of the accident , the aircraft sustained 19,329 flight hours and 8,841 pressurization cycles ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d01", "start": 549, "end": 596, "text": "[ 1 ] Crew 72 passengers were aboard the flight"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d02", "start": 0, "end": 294, "text": "Sudan Airways Flight 109 Sudan Airways Flight 109 was an international scheduled Amman–Damascus–Khartoum passenger service, operated with an Airbus A310, that crashed on landing at Khartoum International Airport on 10 June 2008, approximately at 17:00 UTC, killing 30 of 214 occupants on board."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d02", "start": 295, "end": 433, "text": "The aircraft involved in the accident was an Airbus A310-324, c/n 548, tail number that had its maiden flight on 23 August 1990 as F-WWCV."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d02", "start": 434, "end": 558, "text": "Equipped with a twin-PW4152 powerplant, it was delivered new to Singapore Airlines on 22 October 1990 and registered 9V-STU."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d02", "start": 559, "end": 628, "text": "Re-registered VT-EVF, it was delivered to Air India on 10 March 2001."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d02", "start": 629, "end": 632, "text": "The"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d03", "start": 0, "end": 119, "text": "at Khartoum International Airport on 10 June 2008 , approximately at 17:00 UTC , killing 30 of 214 occupants on board ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d03", "start": 120, "end": 279, "text": "Aircraft The aircraft involved in the accident was an Airbus A310-324 , c/n 548 , tail number ST-ATN , that had its maiden flight on 23 August 1990 as F-WWCV ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d03", "start": 280, "end": 406, "text": "Equipped with a twin-PW4152 powerplant , it was delivered new to Singapore Airlines on 22 October 1990 and registered 9V-STU ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d03", "start": 407, "end": 478, "text": "Re-registered VT-EVF , it was delivered to Air India on 10 March 2001 ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d03", "start": 479, "end": 554, "text": "The aircraft was finally registered ST-ATN , and delivered to Sudan Airways"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d04", "start": 0, "end": 372, "text": "von Luftfahrt-Zwischenfällen Der Sudan-Airways-Flug 109 ( Flugnummer IATA : SD109 , ICAO : SUD109 , Funkrufzeichen : SUDANAIR 109 ) war ein internationaler Linien inlandsflug der Fluggesellschaft Sudan Airways vom Flughafen Amman zum Flughafen Khartum mit einem planmäßigen Zwischenstopp auf dem Flughafen Damaskus und einem außerplanmäßigen auf dem Flughafen Port Sudan ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d04", "start": 373, "end": 380, "text": "Am 10 ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d04", "start": 381, "end": 553, "text": "Juni 2008 verunfallte auf diesem Flug ein Airbus A310-324 mit dem Luftfahrzeugkennzeichen ST-ATN , nachdem er bei der Landung in Khartum das Landebahnende überrollt hatte ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d04", "start": 554, "end": 654, "text": "Bei der anschließenden chaotischen Evakuierung der brennenden Maschine starben 30 der 214 Insassen ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0286-3b46f8a7bf53:d04", "start": 655, "end": 695, "text": "Inhaltsverzeichnis 1 Maschine 2 Insassen"}, "D6S1": {